## Proposed Solution for Issue #261

### Root Cause Analysis & Fix
The digest generator was reading the markdown file with `readline()` which stops at the first newline, so only the first sentence of the daily digest was ever rendered. Switching to a full‑file read (`fs.readFileSync(..., 'utf8')`) loads the entire markdown, allowing the complete digest to be processed and displayed.

### Proposed Code Patch
```
--- a/src/digest.js
+++ b/src/digest.js
@@
-const fs = require('fs');
-const readline = require('readline');
-
-/**
- * Load the daily digest markdown file.
- * Previously used `readline` which only returned the first line.
- */
-function loadDigest(path) {
-  const rl = readline.createInterface({
-    input: fs.createReadStream(path),
-    crlfDelay: Infinity,
-  });
-  return new Promise((resolve) => {
-    let content = '';
-    rl.on('line', (line) => {
-      content += line + '\n';
-    });
-    rl.on('close', () => resolve(content));
-  });
-}
+const fs = require('fs');
+
+/**
+ * Load the daily digest markdown file.
+ * Uses `fs.readFileSync` to read the whole file as UTF‑8 text, ensuring the
+ * complete digest is returned instead of only the first line.
+ */
+function loadDigest(path) {
+  return fs.readFileSync(path, 'utf8');
+}
*** End of File ***
```

