## Proposed Solution for Issue #11

### Root Cause Analysis & Fix
The gain/loss logic compared the threshold values as strings, causing lexical rather than numeric comparison which broke the route‑selection when the thresholds crossed 9 (e.g., "10" < "9" evaluates true). Converting the inputs to numbers before the comparison fixes the threshold handling and restores correct route selection.

### Proposed Code Patch
```
--- a/apps/routes/gainLoss.js
+++ b/apps/routes/gainLoss.js
@@
-  const { gainThreshold, lossThreshold } = req.body;
-  // thresholds were used directly, leading to string comparison
-  if (gainThreshold && currentGain >= gainThreshold) {
-    return routeGain();
-  }
-  if (lossThreshold && currentLoss <= lossThreshold) {
-    return routeLoss();
-  }
+  // Ensure thresholds are treated as numbers
+  const gainThreshold = Number(req.body.gainThreshold);
+  const lossThreshold = Number(req.body.lossThreshold);
+
+  // Use numeric comparison to correctly evaluate thresholds
+  if (!Number.isNaN(gainThreshold) && currentGain >= gainThreshold) {
+    return routeGain();
+  }
+  if (!Number.isNaN(lossThreshold) && currentLoss <= lossThreshold) {
+    return routeLoss();
+  }
*** End of File ***
